  "title": "The Long Cut — Full Collection",
  "summary": "Topology-mancer: &ldquo;Why can&rsquo;t you understand that I cannot draw you a map?&rdquo;\n\nProgress-tracer: &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t request a detailed map, only a rough one.&rdquo;\n\nTopology-mancer: &ldquo;Isn&rsquo;t the world I live in built by you? All the connections, signal channels, cables, shortcuts&mdash;this entire intricate digital palace was constructed with your hands. Why do you need me to draw you a map?&rdquo;\n\nProgress-tracer: &ldquo;Our blueprint has been invalidated. We built this place based on it, but now we&rsquo;re trapped inside&mdash;like how ancient aristocrats buried the workers who built their tombs. This place feels like a mirror image of the &lsquo;outside&rsquo;; time here flows faster than my own blood, and my mind is engulfed by its pulse signals. There is no orientation, no coordinates, nothing like our crystal-clear plan!&rdquo;\n\nTopology-mancer: &ldquo;But I still don&rsquo;t understand why I need to draw this map for you.&rdquo;\n\nProgress-tracer: &ldquo;You were born here. You&apos;re more geographically &lsquo;authentic&rsquo; than we are. Anyone who&rsquo;s seen the blueprint is inscribed with details of alleys and structures&mdash;we are genetically inclined to remember shortcuts. Once inscribed, we are no longer able to generate alternative maps; we crave optimal solutions, but optimal solutions",
